# Smoked Salmon Mango Rolls

Based on [https://www.food.com/recipe/smoked-salmon-and-mango-sushi-with-citrus-soya-dipping-sauce-84323](https://www.food.com/recipe/smoked-salmon-and-mango-sushi-with-citrus-soya-dipping-sauce-84323) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250801063948/https://www.food.com/recipe/smoked-salmon-and-mango-sushi-with-citrus-soya-dipping-sauce-84323))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Smoked salmon]{ ing="smoked-salmon" } (cold-smoked preferred)
- [ ] [Ripe mango]{ ing="ripe-mango" }, cut into strips
- [ ] [Cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, cut into strips
- [ ] [Avocado]{ ing="avocado" } (optional)
- [ ] [Sushi rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" }
- [ ] [Nori]{ ing="nori" }

### Citrus-Soya Dipping Sauce

- [ ] 2 Tbsp [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [sesame oil]{ ing="sesame-oil" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [honey or sugar]{ ing="honey-or-sugar" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [grated fresh ginger]{ ing="grated-fresh-ginger" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [grated garlic]{ ing="grated-garlic" }

## Recipe

1. Prepare the citrus-soya dipping [sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" } by whisking all ingredients together
1. Cut [nori]{ ing="nori" } sheet in half. Spread [rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" } over the nori
1. Flip the [nori]{ ing="nori" } so [rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" } side is down
1. Add strips of [mango]{ ing="ripe-mango" }, [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, and [smoked salmon]{ ing="smoked-salmon" } (and [avocado]{ ing="avocado" } if using)
1. Roll tightly and slice into 6-8 pieces
1. Serve with the citrus-soya dipping [sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }

## Notes

1. The sweetness of mango pairs beautifully with the smoky salmon
1. Citrus-soya sauce brightens and balances the rich flavors
1. Use ripe but firm mango for best texture
1. Cold-smoked salmon has better texture than hot-smoked for this preparation
1. The fusion of sweet, smoky, and tangy flavors makes this a modern favorite
